{"author":{"id":"5698b6d16d951325374257d86a2e673da0e55970c3d21c0f7c6f49018f24e5bf"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1787116572,"nonce":"DzP+TG0IaPluekHe7R+IdW8PFaU=","message":"Fixed in `77886a8` (pushed to `main`), with **one Done-when clause refused on evidence** — see below.\n\n\nThe diagnosis in this ticket was right. `snoozed` and `unsnoozed` are the only two Reasons a snooze may not suppress (§B.8.4), so both reach a real channel at every verbosity, and the Slack renderer had no branch for either: `replyBody` fell to `default:` and posted `:information_source: *Title* — :fire: Firing`, while `reasonPhrase` returned `\"\"` so the amended root changed with no clause saying why.\n\n- `NotificationView.SnoozedUntil`, filled by `ViewService.project` from the snapshot the repository was already joining. `Actor` (who) and `Comment` (the note) were already projected — the until-when was the only fact the renderer could not reach.\n- `snoozed` / `unsnoozed` arms in `replyBody`, `replyLead`, `replyFacts`, `reasonPhrase`, `trailEmoji`, `trailVerb`.\n- §B.8.6's `*Notifications*\\n:zzz: Snoozed by \u003c@U…\u003e until \u003c!date^…\u003e` field on the root card.\n- The push text leads with the snooze: `:zzz: Snoozed: OtoSmokeTest on smoke-test. Severity critical, team observability, oto quiet until 22:02 UTC.` — it was `:bell: Update on: … firing since 17:56 UTC.`\n- Both goldens re-cut, `reply_unsnoozed` / `root_unsnoozed` added, and the comments in `golden_test.go` **and** `test/harness/slack_cards.go` rewritten from \"evidence of a defect, fix withheld\" to a record of the decision.\n\n\nThe SPEC binds the opposite, and §P-17 asks for a golden proving the *current* colour:\n\n- `docs/design/SPEC.md:3935-3940` (§H.4 call-out): *\"⛔ Snooze does NOT change the card's colour or emoji … A snoozed firing critical stays `#a30200` / `:rotating_light:` … Colouring a snoozed critical calm would be the exact lie §E.1.1 exists to prevent.\"*\n- `:633-634` (§B.8.6): *\"Colour and leading emoji are UNCHANGED. They follow `case.state`.\"*\n- `:553` (§B.8.1): *\"every surface MUST continue to render it that way (§B.8.6).\"*\n- `:590` (§B.8.2): *\"Colour and status field follow `case.state` (the world).\"*\n- `:6166` (§P-17): *\"colour and severity emoji unchanged while snoozed — **add a golden file proving a snoozed critical still renders `#a30200`**.\"*\n- `internal/notification/domain/snapshot.go:195-197`: *\"a snoozed critical is still rendered as a firing critical.\"*\n\nIt was mechanically blocked too: `TestSlackPaletteUnchanged` reads §H.2 off the SPEC and fails on a hex `palette.go` uses that §H.2 does not sanction, so a new snooze colour would need §H.2 amended — i.e. reversing a recorded ruling to satisfy a ticket that did not cite it.\n\nSnooze is the **third orthogonal axis**: a fact about oto's notification behaviour, not about the world, and the colour reports the world. So the colour stays `#a30200` on all four cards, and `TestGoldenSnoozedCriticalKeepsTheFiringColour` was added — §P-17's own acceptance criterion, written down at last. The defect was always words, and it is fixed in words.\n\n\nThe first cut rendered the until-when with a bare clock (`plainClock` / `slackDate`'s `{time}`). Every other timestamp on these cards points backward, where that is unambiguous; a snooze points forward up to 30 days (§B.8.3), so *\"oto quiet until 22:02 UTC\"* on a seven-day snooze reads as tonight — a false statement to the person who set it. New `plainMoment` adds the day only when it differs, the block moved to `slackDateTime`, and `TestALongSnoozeNamesTheDayAndNotJustTheClock` pins both directions.\n\n\n| | |\n|---|---|\n| reply says who / until when / not firing | ✅ `grep -io firing` over `reply_snoozed.golden.json` returns nothing |\n| neither card firing-red | ⛔ **refused**, citations above |\n| `unsnoozed` audible again, distinguishable from a state change | ✅ |\n| goldens re-cut, comment no longer describes a defect | ✅ (both `golden_test.go` and `slack_cards.go`) |\n| `NotificationView` carries the snooze | ✅ `just lint-reachability` green proves production write *and* read |\n| fallback text names the snooze | ✅ |\n\n\nRun individually — `just ci` aborts at the known-red `lint-vocabulary` and never reaches `test`. `lint`, `lint-reachability`, `dto-check`, `server-check`, `generate-check`, `validators-check`, `ui-build`, `ui-test` all exit 0. `lint-vocabulary` output byte-identical to baseline (60). `just test`: no new failures; `internal/channels/render/slack` and `test/arch` green.\n\n\n§B.8.6's `Snooze` → `:bell: Unsnooze` action swap. `v.Actions` is built by `ViewService.actions`, outside this change's boundary and not required by any Done-when clause. Worth its own ticket.","files":null}]}